 {"language": {"code": "th", "name": "Thai"}, "word": "โป๊กเกอร์"}, {"language": {"code": "th", "name": "Thai"}, "word": "เผ"}, {"language": {"code": "tr", "name": "Turkish"}, "word": "poker"}, {"language": {"code": "uk", "name": "Ukrainian"}, "word": "по́кер"}, {"language": {"code": "ur", "name": "Urdu"}, "word": "پوکر"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "pôke"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "bài xì"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(soccer, rare) The scoring of four goals by a player in one match.", "tags": ["countable", "rare", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Greaves hit three hat-tricks, two pokers and five goals against West Brom on his way to a record-setting 41 league goals.", "reference": "2021 September 20, Ratul Ghosh, “THE BEST MOMENTS FROM JIMMY GREAVES' LEGENDARY FOOTBALLING CAREER”, in FootTheBall:"}, {"text": "Poker Face: Taty Castellanos strikes FOUR times for NYCFC vs. RSL", "reference": "2022 April 17, Dylan Butler, “Recap: NYCFC 6, Real Salt Lake 0”, in MLS:"}, {"text": "Ibra has scored a \"poker\" on four separate occasions during his career: twice with Paris Saint-Germain and twice for Sweden. The most famed example must surely be his single-handed crushing of England in a friendly back in 2012, when the striker rounded off a 4-2 victory for the Swedes with a truly immense long-range overhead kick in the final minute.", "reference": "2023 January 24, Chris Wright, “Mbappe scored career-high five goals in one game. What about Messi, Ronaldo and world's other top strikers?”, in ESPN:"}, {"text": "The only player who scored a poker at Nou Camp is Milinko Pantić. Curiously, despite his 4 goals, his team (Atlético Madrid) lost the game.", "reference": "2023 April 6, “THE 11TH HAT TRICK SCORER AT NOU CAMP”, in International Federation of Football History and Statistics:"}, {"text": "Daka also became only the fifth player to score four or more in a Europa League match, and the second fastest after Willian José, whose 'poker' came in the space of 26 minutes for Real Sociedad at Vardar in 2017.", "reference": "2023 April 30, “Europa League's fastest goals and quickest hat-tricks”, in UEFA:"}], "synonyms": ["haul"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["poker"], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈpoʊkɚ/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈpəʊkə/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}], "forms": [{"word": "pokers", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "pokering", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "pokered", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "pokered", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To play poker.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Then we went to Mead's and pokered until morning.", "reference": "1929, West Virginia Wild Life, page 38:"}, {"text": "Papa liked nothing better than a game of poker . His pokering habits caused Mama grave anxiety.", "reference": "1969, Emma Wilson Emery, Aunt Puss & Others: Old Days in the Piney Woods, page 94:"}, {"text": "\"He ran with and pokered with us boys,” Bob Paine would recall fifty years later, “ the darndest, pepperyest, finest companion a fellow could ask.”", "reference": "1992, Vance H. Trimble, The Astonishing Mr. Scripps, page 56:"}, {"text": "“Yeah,” Lemming mutters. “We're pokering, so shut the fuck up.” “I raise five,” Blake announces.", "reference": "2017, Elle Kennedy, Sarina Bowen, Stay:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈpoʊkɚ/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈpəʊkə/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}], "forms": [{"word": "pokers", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(US, colloquial) Any imagined frightful object, especially one supposed to haunt the darkness; a bugbear.", "tags": ["US", "colloquial"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The very leaves on the horse-chesnuts[…]cling to the bough as if old poker was coming to take them away.", "reference": "5 May 1784, Horace Walpole, letter to Hon. H. S. Conway:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["poker"], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poker", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}